---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Command from '../components/Command.astro';
import { INSTALL_CMD, INSTALL_URL, GET_STARTED_URL } from '../data/commands';
---

<Layout title="Install ucli" description="Install the ucli tool manager with one command">
  <div class="u-wrap"><div class="u-page u-ipage">
    <h1>Install ucli</h1>
    <p class="u-lede">One command builds ucli at its pinned commit and puts it in <code>~/.local/bin</code>. A new install never asks for sudo.</p>
    <Command bar label="Install" cmd={INSTALL_CMD}>
      <p class="u-install__note">Linux and macOS; on Windows, use WSL. You need curl, git, make and bash. ucli is a bash script, so install bash first if you lack it. If ucli is already in <code>/usr/local/bin</code>, it is updated there, which may ask for your password; <code>ucli install --move</code> moves it to <code>~/.local/bin</code>.</p>
    </Command>
    <p class="u-next"><a href={INSTALL_URL}>Read the script</a><a href={GET_STARTED_URL}>Quick start</a></p>

    <div class="u-ibody">
      <section class="u-ib">
        <h2>What the installer does</h2>
        <ol class="u-ilist">
          <li>Checks that curl, git, make and bash are installed, and says what to install if not.</li>
          <li>Reads the commit the registry pins for ucli, and fetches exactly that commit from <a href="https://github.com/ucli-tools/ucli">github.com/ucli-tools/ucli</a>.</li>
          <li>Builds it and puts <code>ucli</code> in <code>~/.local/bin</code>. A new install never asks for sudo; an existing <code>/usr/local/bin/ucli</code> is updated where it is, which may ask for your password.</li>
          <li>Tells you if <code>~/.local/bin</code> is missing from your <code>PATH</code>, and how to add it for bash, zsh or fish.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="u-ib">
        <h2>Read it before you run it</h2>
        <p>Download it, read it, check it, then run it:</p>
        <Command label="Read the installer first" lines={[
          'curl -fsSLO https://install.ucli.tools/install.sh',
          'curl -fsSLO https://install.ucli.tools/install.sh.sha256',
          'less install.sh',
          'sha256sum -c install.sh.sha256',
          { t: '# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c install.sh.sha256', c: true },
          'bash install.sh',
        ]} />
        <p>The check catches a download cut short; it does not protect against a compromised server.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="u-ib">
        <h2>Check that it worked</h2>
        <p>Open a new terminal and ask ucli for its version. Then build your first tool.</p>
        <Command label="Check the install" lines={['ucli --version', 'ucli build mdtexpdf']} />
        <p class="u-more">To remove ucli later, run <code>ucli uninstall</code>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</Layout>
